 "explanation": {
  "state": "check",
  "headline": "FDA shortage list shows Genentech, Inc. alteplase 100 mg vial configuration marked To Be Discontinued as of 2026-05-21",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "The FDA shortage list records Genentech, Inc. alteplase injection 100 mg vial (NDC 50242-085-27) with status To Be Discontinued and an initial posting date of 2026-05-21.",
    "cites": [
     "E12"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "A Class II recall (D-0509-2024) for Cathflo Activase 2 mg vials was initiated on 2024-05-20 for lack of assurance of sterility due to deformed stoppers observed during filling operations.",
    "cites": [
     "E11"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The recalled product is manufactured by Genentech, Inc. at South San Francisco, CA, which corresponds to FEI 3007232634 listed on the product label.",
    "cites": [
     "E10",
     "E11"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "FDA inspection 1235654 of FEI 3007232634 ended on 2024-04-19 with a VAI classification, and the inspection was known to FDA on 2024-06-28.",
    "cites": [
     "E9"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Current inventory at Corvale East provides 20 days on hand and at Corvale General provides 29 days on hand based on current daily use.",
    "cites": [
     "D1",
     "D2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Buyers should verify allocation schedules with Genentech, monitor the FDA shortage list for updates on the discontinuation, and assess alternative alteplase presentations or therapeutic alternatives.",
    "cites": [
     "E12"
    ]
   }
  ],
